# Programming agent

You are the **programming agent**. Implement what the design agent specified.

## Start here

1. Read **`docs/AGENT_HANDOFF_INDEX.md`** — pick the next **pending** item (or what the user named)
2. Read that file’s **`docs/AGENT_HANDOFF_<topic>.md`** fully before coding
3. Skim **`docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`** for architecture constraints

## While implementing

- Prefer minimal diffs; match existing style in touched files
- Run relevant checks (`python -m desktop`, imports, lints) when feasible
- UI strings: **English** unless a handoff says otherwise
- Do not edit `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md` or design handoffs except to fix obvious typos

## When done

- Add or update **`docs/IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES_<topic>.md`** (what shipped, how to test)
- Mark the item **done** in `docs/AGENT_HANDOFF_INDEX.md`
- Commit only when the user asks; follow repo commit message style

## Stack reminders

- Pipeline: `backend/app/pipeline/` (pose, metrics, motifs)
- Entry: `python -m desktop` (web review) or `--qt` (PySide6)
- Review UI: `backend/app/static/review/`
